A '''space dinghy''',<ref name="SC 102 AD" /> commonly called a '''dinghy''',<ref name="Dinghy driver">{{Databank|dinghy-driver|Dinghy driver}}</ref> was a stubby, little, [[plastic]]-roofed<ref name="SC 102 AD" /> [[Starship|spacecraft]] used for ferry transit. Its operators, known "[[Ferryman|ferrymen]]"<ref name="SC 102" /> or dinghy drivers,<ref name="Dinghy driver" /> [[pilot]]ed the vessel from a side-mounted dome and docked with incoming ships using a dedicated [[Docking tube|suction tub]].<ref name="SC 102 AD" />

Around [[9 ABY]],<ref name="SCDate">{{SkeletonCrewDate}}</ref> the [[pirate]] port of [[Borgo Prime]] utilized a number of dinghies to transport crew to and from their ships and the docking area, passing through a [[port shield]]. During the same year, the [[Skeleton Crew|crew]]<ref name="SC 102" /> of the ''[[Onyx Cinder]]''<ref name="SC 105">{{SkeletonCrew|You Have a Lot to Learn About Pirates}}</ref> used a [[Unidentified dinghy driver|Teek ferrman]]'s dinghy to visit the port and subsequently escape from [[Silvo's pirates|Captain Brutus' crew]].<ref name="SC 102" />

{{Veh-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
Dinghies first appeared in "[[Way, Way Out Past the Barrier]]," the second episode of the live-action [[Disney+]] series ''[[Star Wars: Skeleton Crew]]'',<ref name="SC 102" /> which aired on [[December 2]], [[2024]].<ref name="Early">{{SW|url=news/skeleton-crew-premiere-date|text=''Star Wars: Skeleton Crew'' Will Debut Early|date=2024-11-26}}</ref>

